  "description": "Florida's 24th Congressional District is an open seat following the retirement of Democratic incumbent Frederica Wilson, who has held the seat since 2011. The district, which covers parts of Miami-Dade and Broward counties including Miami Gardens, Hollywood, and Miramar, is heavily Democratic. A crowded Democratic primary featuring several well-known local officials and political heirs will likely determine the next representative. The race takes place under a new congressional map drawn by Governor Ron DeSantis that is expected to give Republicans a 24-4 advantage statewide, but this district remains safely Democratic.",
